<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#new-economic-mechanism">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Economic Mechanism</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Economic Mechanism is the name of market-oriented reforms in two communist states. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, introduced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janos-kadar">János Kádár</a>'s government in 1968, it gave state enterprises more freedom and allowed some market prices, making Hungary the most liberal economy in the Soviet bloc. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, from 1986, it opened the economy to private enterprise and foreign investment.</p></div>
